# Vendored binaries must stay BYTE-EXACT.
#
# .github/boot-template/magiskboot-x86_64 is a static x86_64 ELF that the pack step copies
# and checks against a pinned sha256. If git is allowed to apply core.autocrlf to it, the
# working tree copy (and therefore the copy CI checks out) gains CR bytes and the run dies
# with "does not match the pinned sha256". Marked binary so git never touches its contents.
#
# The same reasoning applies to every other blob in boot-template: the stock boot image is
# gzipped and the header template is raw binary.
.github/boot-template/magiskboot-x86_64 binary
.github/boot-template/*.bin binary
.github/boot-template/*.gz binary
